From 740b5282aa29d2ac65095290304f359f8be00c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:18:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] macos-arm64: asynchronous ray tracing with reprojected
 composite

The depth captured at frame N is traced at N+1 (after a GL fence, never a
finish) and composited at N+2 by a GL shader that reconstructs each pixel's
world position from the current depth, projects it into the traced frame and
takes the depth-nearest half-resolution sample. Three rotating slots of
IOSurfaces; the Metal composite kernel is gone. The GPU now overlaps the GL
frame with the tracer instead of the render thread stalling twice per frame:
176 fps instead of ~100 at 1512x982 with AO, dynamic objects and shadows.
Instance lists are keyed by frame so a slot is traced with the objects of its
own frame. rt_async 0 restores the synchronous path.
